---
import { fatalWasteSlopeEvents, trashMountainMediaBase } from "@/data/trash-mountain";
---

<section class="case-ledger article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="case-ledger-title">
  <header>
    <div>
      <p>Working audit, September 1996–July 2026</p>
      <h2 id="case-ledger-title">Twenty-two fatal waste-slope failures</h2>
    </div>
    <a class="download" href={`${trashMountainMediaBase}/data/fatal-waste-slope-events.csv`} download>
      Download CSV
    </a>
  </header>

  <div class="ledger-summary">
    <article>
      <strong>691</strong>
      <span>conservative confirmed total in the audited ledger</span>
    </article>
    <article>
      <strong>751</strong>
      <span>if Payatas uses the engineering account’s 278 recovered bodies</span>
    </article>
    <article>
      <strong>10</strong>
      <span>events reached occupied residential areas</span>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p class="ledger-caveat">
    This is an audited working inventory, not a complete world registry. Confirmed and missing people remain separate. The 691 total uses the later three-death Rodriguez account; the strongest official update located still reported one confirmed death and two missing people.
  </p>

  <details>
    <summary>Open the full event ledger</summary>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Date</th>
            <th scope="col">Site and place</th>
            <th scope="col">Confirmed deaths</th>
            <th scope="col">Missing</th>
            <th scope="col">Homes reached</th>
            <th scope="col">Confidence</th>
            <th scope="col">Receipt</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {fatalWasteSlopeEvents.map((event) => (
            <tr class:list={[event.confidence.includes("low") && "is-provisional"]}>
              <td data-label="Date"><time datetime={event.date}>{event.date}</time></td>
              <td data-label="Site and place">
                <strong>{event.site}</strong>
                <span>{event.place}, {event.country}</span>
                <small>{event.note}</small>
              </td>
              <td data-label="Confirmed">{event.confirmed}</td>
              <td data-label="Missing">{event.missing ?? "—"}</td>
              <td data-label="Homes reached"><span class:list={["home-status", `is-${event.reachedHomes}`]}>{event.reachedHomes}</span></td>
              <td data-label="Confidence">{event.confidence}</td>
              <td data-label="Receipt"><a href={event.sourceUrl} rel="noreferrer">Source</a></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>

  <footer>
    Residential means the moving waste reached occupied houses or a settlement. “Mass-casualty neighborhood” in the audit means at least six confirmed resident deaths. Those are editorial classifications, not international standards.
  </footer>
</section>

<style>
  .case-ledger {
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgb(163 200 111 / 0.32);
    border-radius: 0.65rem;
    background: #0a0c09;
  }

  header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
    background: linear-gradient(110deg, rgb(70 99 43 / 0.52), transparent 64%);
  }

  header p,
  header h2 {
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  header p {
    color: #b2df80 !important;
    font: 700 0.68rem/1.2 var(--font-mono), monospace !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  header h2 {
    margin-top: 0.35rem !important;
    color: #f1f5e8 !important;
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 2rem) !important;
  }

  .download {
    flex: none;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem;
    color: #d7f0b8;
    border: 1px solid rgb(178 223 128 / 0.45);
    border-radius: 0.3rem;
    font: 700 0.68rem/1.2 var(--font-mono), monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .download:hover {
    color: #0a0c09;
    background: #b2df80;
  }

  .ledger-summary {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: rgb(163 200 111 / 0.2);
  }

  .ledger-summary article {
    padding: 1rem;
    background: #0d100c;
  }

  .ledger-summary strong {
    display: block;
    color: #d7f0b8;
    font: 700 clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.6rem)/1 var(--font-mono), monospace;
  }

  .ledger-summary span {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
    color: #9fa994;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .ledger-caveat {
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem !important;
    color: #b9c0b2 !important;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.025);
    border-block: 1px solid rgb(163 200 111 / 0.18);
    font: 0.74rem/1.55 var(--font-mono), monospace !important;
  }

  details {
    color: #d6ddd0;
  }

  summary {
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    color: #d7f0b8;
    cursor: pointer;
    font: 700 0.75rem/1.3 var(--font-mono), monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(163 200 111 / 0.18);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0 !important;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    color: #cfd4ca;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  th,
  td {
    padding: 0.75rem 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.08);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  th {
    color: #b2df80;
    background: #10140e;
    font: 700 0.63rem/1.2 var(--font-mono), monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  td strong,
  td span,
  td small {
    display: block;
  }

  td strong {
    color: #f0f2ec;
  }

  td small {
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
    color: #8e9787;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  tr.is-provisional {
    background: rgb(184 122 60 / 0.08);
  }

  .home-status {
    width: max-content;
    padding: 0.18rem 0.32rem;
    border-radius: 0.18rem;
    font: 700 0.62rem/1 var(--font-mono), monospace;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .home-status.is-yes {
    color: #ffd0c3;
    background: rgb(206 91 72 / 0.22);
  }

  .home-status.is-no {
    color: #b2df80;
    background: rgb(113 154 72 / 0.2);
  }

  .home-status.is-unclear {
    color: #f1c48f;
    background: rgb(184 122 60 / 0.2);
  }

  td a {
    color: #b2df80;
    text-underline-offset: 0.14em;
  }

  footer {
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem 1rem;
    color: #879080;
    font: 0.68rem/1.55 var(--font-mono), monospace;
  }

  @media (max-width: 719px) {
    header {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .ledger-summary {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    thead {
      display: none;
    }

    tbody,
    tr,
    td {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    tr {
      padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);
    }

    td {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 7rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.65rem;
      padding: 0.38rem 0;
      border: 0;
    }

    td::before {
      content: attr(data-label);
      color: #7f8d73;
      font: 700 0.62rem/1.4 var(--font-mono), monospace;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
  }
</style>
